I'd mentioned this briefly in another post, but figured I'd throw it out there
for everyone. Maybe it's common, but it sort of took me by suprise. I was down
on what I presumed to be the medusa board (judging from the great number of
statues). To find out if this was indeed the case, I wrapped a towel around my
head to let my ESP do the trick. Sure enough, I found a '@' in the middle of
the level. Just to make sure, I used the '/' command and found out it was 
Medusa. While I was waiting around for the polymorph ring to kick in (I have
control and wanted to become a vampire lord to get across the water - only
found out about the powers of the Heart later, but that's another story), I
noticed that the '@' had disappeared. I was sort of confused and, once I 
'morphed, searched the whole board to see if I could find here. Only upon 
entering her sanctum did I find out what had happened - there was a statue
of Medusa sitting there. Yes, I did have an amulet of reflection, but could
that have done the trick? I was half a screen away and definitely did not have
a line of sight. I only 'saw' her via ESP. Do you think the reflection was 
indeed the cause (if so, is this a feature, bug, or what?)? If not, what
happened?

This isn't really a problem, but it picqued my curiousity.

